A||||4||CUTTER||Problem...starter or fuel pump?||||5||
Z||000000||CUTTER||05-07-2000||10:33 PM||||I have a problem and dont know if its the starter or fuel pump, sometimes (not all of the time) when I turn the key, the motor cranks and then what sounds like the starter whines and I have to let go of the key and try again. it makes a sound like this...<BR>whhhheeeeeeeeeeeemmmmmmmmm.....like the starter is sliping or something. When it happens the motor doesnt crank anymore, I usually can get it started within 3 times, then when it warms up or drive for a while, turn the car off and try to start it again it starts fine. Usually it happens when it was sitting the night, like when I go to work in the morning. Any info would help,<BR>Thanks, Shane||||reg||5
Z||000001||Homicidal||05-07-2000||11:04 PM||||I got a very similiar problem but I don't have a whine.<P>I used a voltmeter and checked my battery and it turns out my battery is going dead.<P>Same problem?||||reg||1
Z||000002||sully5||05-08-2000||08:05 AM||||Cutter, you might also check out the bendix on the starter. Had one go out on my Camaro. However, it would not even crank the motor. Easy enough fix, if that is the prob. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000003||V8Fiero||05-09-2000||08:20 PM||||Sounds like the starter to me. Mine would start grinding and then it would totally let loose and spin. What I did was crawl under the car while it was on jack stands and have my wife try and start the while i looked at the starter to see what it was doing. Just be careful when you are under there. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Homicidal||05-09-2000||09:08 PM||||Or just a loose connection on the starter.<P>That battery problem I mentioned above really was just a loose wire!  Two turns of a ratchet and all problems gone!||||reg||1
